---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import SectionIntro from '../components/SectionIntro.astro';
import ThresholdBlock from '../components/ThresholdBlock.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
import SiteCta from '../components/SiteCta.astro';
import EditorialPhoto from '../components/EditorialPhoto.astro';
import { withBase } from '../data/site';
import openDoorway from '../assets/images/editorial/editorial-open-doorway.png';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Where Are You Standing Right Now? | She Who Remembers"
  description="A quiet way to locate your current threshold: boundaries, self-trust, identity, restlessness. Then choose a course or private guidance."
>
  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="Where are you standing right now?" headingLevel="h1">
        <p>
          You do not have to know which course you need. Start with what feels familiar. The name
          of the work can come later. The texture of this season is enough.
        </p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="photo-breath">
        <EditorialPhoto
          src={openDoorway}
          variant="doorway"
          alt="A wooden door stands open in a plaster room, leading onto a sunlit stone terrace and distant trees."
        />
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <ThresholdBlock
        number="01"
        quote="I am tired of being the strong one."
        pathways={[
          { label: 'The Remembering', href: withBase('/courses/the-remembering') },
          { label: 'Private Guidance', href: withBase('/private-guidance') },
        ]}
      >
        <p>
          You carry. You manage. You anticipate the next need before anyone names it. Solving has
          become so fluent it can look like personality. Competence is a real gift. It can also
          become a room with no windows.
        </p>
        <p>
          Receiving may feel unfamiliar. Self-contact may feel like a luxury you cannot justify.
          The question is not whether you are capable. It is whether capability has replaced
          consultation with yourself.
        </p>
      </ThresholdBlock>

      <Divider variant="ornament" />

      <ThresholdBlock
        number="02"
        quote="I am tired of everyone's shit."
        pathways={[{ label: 'The Sacred No', href: withBase('/courses/the-sacred-no') }]}
      >
        <p>
          There is a moment when patience stops being virtue and starts being self-erasure. You
          can love people and still be done with the unpaid emotional labor, the ignored nos, the
          way your time is treated as public property.
        </p>
        <p>
          Resentment is often a delayed boundary. Anger can be information. The work is not to
          become cruel. It is to tell the truth before the truth has to shout. A clean no is
          different from retaliation. One restores you. The other just rearranges the mess.
        </p>
      </ThresholdBlock>

      <Divider variant="ornament" />

      <ThresholdBlock
        number="03"
        quote="I don't recognize myself anymore."
        pathways={[{ label: 'The Remembering', href: withBase('/courses/the-remembering') }]}
      >
        <p>
          Divorce. Motherhood. Caregiving. Burnout. A career that changed shape. Aging. Grief. An
          identity that no longer answers to the old name. Or no dramatic event at all: only a
          slow, honest mismatch between the woman you are becoming and the one the world still
          expects.
        </p>
        <p>
          Not recognizing yourself is not always collapse. Sometimes it is the first accurate
          sighting in years.
        </p>
      </ThresholdBlock>

      <Divider variant="ornament" />

      <ThresholdBlock
        number="04"
        quote="I know what I should do. I just don't trust myself."
        pathways={[
          { label: 'The Remembering', href: withBase('/courses/the-remembering') },
          { label: 'Private Guidance', href: withBase('/private-guidance') },
        ]}
      >
        <p>
          You can be intelligent and still outsource your knowing. Advice becomes a habit. Another
          podcast, another opinion, another round of overthinking dressed as diligence. Intuition
          and anxiety can feel similar in the body until discernment learns the difference.
        </p>
        <p>
          Self-trust is not stubbornness. It is the capacity to hear yourself without immediately
          putting the decision up for committee.
        </p>
      </ThresholdBlock>

      <Divider variant="ornament" />

      <ThresholdBlock
        number="05"
        quote="My life is fine. So why am I restless?"
        pathways={[{ label: 'Legacy in Motion', href: withBase('/courses/legacy-in-motion') }]}
      >
        <p>
          Gratitude and expansion are not enemies. You can love what you have and still feel the
          next true thing knocking. Restlessness is not always a character flaw. Sometimes it is
          unused life, asking for a more honest assignment.
        </p>
      </ThresholdBlock>

      <Divider variant="ornament" />

      <ThresholdBlock
        number="06"
        quote="I want support, but I don't want another guru."
        pathways={[{ label: 'Private Guidance', href: withBase('/private-guidance') }]}
      >
        <p>
          The purpose of guidance is not to make the guide more important. It is to make your own
          discernment increasingly available to you. Support should return you to yourself, not
          replace the inner authority you came here to recover.
        </p>
      </ThresholdBlock>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <SiteCta
    heading="You do not need to know exactly what you need before beginning."
    primary={{ label: 'Book a Fit Conversation', href: withBase('/book-a-conversation') }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Explore the Work', href: withBase('/the-work') }}
  >
    <p>
      If more than one threshold sounds like you, that is ordinary. Choose the sentence that
      feels most true today. The rest can wait.
    </p>
  </SiteCta>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .photo-breath {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>
